# Sub-agent token discipline (C18)

**Goal:** lower Cursor token use, faster loops, fewer wrong turns. Do **not** ban sub-agents — **re-scope** them.

## Core rules

1. **Sub-agents = context tool**, not labour-split. Research / explore / audit → **short summary** to parent.
2. **Write, edit, debug, commit** in the **parent/main thread** (Composer-pool).
3. **Never** cold-start a new implementer per failed attempt. Retry in-thread or **resume** the same agent with failure notes.
4. If a sub-agent must implement (rare): **resumable** only; pass prior errors; no re-explore from zero.
5. **Never Auto**; **Composer-pool only** (C4). No API-pool implementer sub-agents.

## Bounded scout briefs (mandatory shape)

Scout/Task prompts must include:

```text
Paths (max 3): …
Goal: …
Return: ≤15 lines — findings + file refs only. No code dumps. No implementation.
```

- Prefer **one** focused scout; parallel scouts **only** when scopes are independent and non-overlapping.
- After scout returns: **parent implements immediately** — do not open another implementer agent for the same work.

## Resume with failure notes

When resuming or retrying:

```text
Previous attempt failed because: …
Already tried: …
Do not re-read whole repo — use prior summary + these paths: …
```

## Do / Don’t

| Do | Don’t |
|----|--------|
| Scout → ≤15-line summary → parent implements | New implementer sub-agent every retry |
| Resume with failure notes | Cold-start that re-derives the same understanding |
| Sequential scout when dependent | Parallel overlapping explores |
| Small, testable parent edits | Split every file across new Tasks |

## PM / parent

- Prefer scout briefs over implementer labour-splits.
- Token discipline overrides “always delegate implementation to specialists.”
- Keep milestones small so parent context stays accurate (see orchestration / PM).
- **Loop escape (C4):** after 2+ failures on the same issue on the cheap model, one escalated attempt on next-cheapest Composer-pool model, then **revert** to cheap default.

